    <edge source="dome" target="hills" id="0">
      <data key="d2">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">All around the dome lay hills mangy with melting snow</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac Asimov" target="Astounding" id="0">
      <data key="d2">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">I had sold five stories to John Campbell, editor of Astounding</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac Asimov" target="Nightfall" id="0">
      <data key="d2">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">the fifth story, "Nightfall," was about to appear</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac Asimov" target="Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d2">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">On August 11, 1941, therefore, I began the story of that interregnum and called it "Foundation."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac Asimov" target="Fred Pohl" id="0">
      <data key="d2">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">had I not had a conversation with Fred Pohl on November 2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac Asimov" target="Campbell" id="0">
      <data key="d2">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">I got to Campbell's, and my enthusiasm must have been catching for Campbell blazed up as I had never seen him do.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac Asimov" target="Doubleday" id="0">
      <data key="d2">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d3">0.8</data>
      <data key="d4">Doubleday (which had already published a science-fiction novel by me, and which had contracted for another)</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac Asimov" target="The Foundation Trilogy" id="0">
      <data key="d2">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">The Foundation series was nominated, and I felt that was going to have to be glory enough for me, since I was sure that Tolkien's "Lord of the Rings" would win. It didn't. The Foundation series won, and the Hugo I received for it has been sitting on my bookcase in the livingroom ever since.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac Asimov" target="Columbia University" id="0">
      <data key="d2">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">I was 21 years old, a graduate student in chemistry at Columbia University</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac Asimov" target="Boston University School of Medicine" id="0">
      <data key="d2">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">I was on the biochemistry faculty of Boston University School of Medicine</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac Asimov" target="FOUNDATION trilogy" id="0">
      <data key="d2">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">ISAAC ASIMOV brings to a close his thousand-year epic of the far future, the FOUNDATION trilogy.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Galactic Empire" target="Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d2">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">I began the story of that interregnum and called it "Foundation." In it, I described how the psychohistorian, Hari Seldon, established a pair of Foundations at opposite ends of the Universe under such circumstances as to make sure that the forces of history would bring about the second Empire after one thousand years instead of the thirty thousand that would be required otherwise.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Foundation" target="Astounding" id="0">
      <data key="d2">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">"Foundation" appeared in the May 1942 issue of Astounding</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Foundation" target="May 1942 issue of Astounding" id="0">
      <data key="d2">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">"Foundation" appeared in the May 1942 issue of As tounding</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Foundation" target="Isaac Asimov" id="0">
      <data key="d2">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">I had spent eight years on the Foundation, written nine stories</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Foundation" target="Galaxy" id="0">
      <data key="d2">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.8</data>
      <data key="d4">It is as far from belief as the outer galaxies from here.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Foundation" target="Galactic dominion" id="0">
      <data key="d2">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.8</data>
      <data key="d4">The Foundation itself told you they aimed at Galactic dominion?</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Foundation" target="ENTITY" id="0">
      <data key="d2">LOCATION</data>
      <data key="d3">1.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The Foundation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Foundation" target="ancient province of Anacreon" id="0">
      <data key="d2">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">The area of the Galaxy indicated falls within the ancient province of Anacreon</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Foundation" target="worlds" id="0">
      <data key="d2">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.8</data>
      <data key="d4">On the worlds that five years previously had known the Foundation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Foundation" target="First Citizen" id="0">
      <data key="d2">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">He might have established his capital on the Foundation, the strongest of his now-conquered enemies</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hari Seldon" target="Foundations" id="0">
      <data key="d2">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">I described how the psychohistorian, Hari Seldon, established a pair of Foundations at opposite ends of the Universe</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hari Seldon" target="psychohistory" id="0">
      <data key="d2">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
