    </edge>
    <edge source="The Foundation Trilogy" target="Hugo" id="0">
      <data key="d2">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">The Foundation series was nominated, and I felt that was going to have to be glory enough for me, since I was sure that Tolkien's "Lord of the Rings" would win. It didn't. The Foundation series won, and the Hugo I received for it has been sitting on my bookcase in the livingroom ever since.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="The Foundation Trilogy" target="sentences" id="0">
      <data key="d2">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">I came across some sentences by science-fiction writer and critic, James Gunn, who, in connection with the Foundation series, said</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="The Foundation Trilogy" target="Trilogy" id="0">
      <data key="d2">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">Action and romance have little to do with the success of the Trilogy – virtually all the action takes place offstage, and the romance is almost invisible – but the stories provide a detective-story fascination with the permutations and reversals of ideas.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="World Science Fiction Convention" target="Cleveland" id="0">
      <data key="d2">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">the World Science Fiction Convention for that year (to be held in Cleveland)</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Tolkien" target="Lord of the Rings" id="0">
      <data key="d2">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">Tolkien's "Lord of the Rings"</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lester del Rey" target="Isaac" id="0">
      <data key="d2">FRIENDS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">my good friend, the great science-fiction writer, Lester del Rey.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lester del Rey" target="Larry Ashmead" id="0">
      <data key="d2">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d3">0.8</data>
      <data key="d4">He even told Larry Ashmead, then my editor at Doubleday, that if I refused to write more Foundation stories, he, Lester, would be willing to take on the task.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac" target="Doubleday" id="0">
      <data key="d2">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">Larry Ashmead, then my editor at Doubleday</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac" target="Lightning Rod" id="0">
      <data key="d2">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">I called it "Lightning Rod" and managed to write fourteen pages</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac" target="The Foundation Trilogy" id="0">
      <data key="d2">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">The Foundation series had been written at a time when our knowledge of astronomy was primitive compared with what it is today.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac" target="Foundations at Bay" id="0">
      <data key="d2">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">I suggested Foundations at Bay, therefore, and that may be the title that will actually be used.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac" target="Hugh O'Neill" id="0">
      <data key="d2">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d3">0.8</data>
      <data key="d4">I brought the manuscript to Hugh O'Neill in batches, and the poor fellow went half-crazy since he insisted on reading it in this broken fashion.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Cathleen Jordan" target="Doubleday" id="0">
      <data key="d2">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">Cathleen Jordan, then my editor at Doubleday</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hugh O'Neill" target="Doubleday" id="0">
      <data key="d2">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">Hugh O'Neill, then my editor there</data>
    </edge>
