      <data key="d4">TO: BEL RIOSE, MILITARY GOVERNOR OF SIWENNA. GENERAL OF THE IMPERIAL FORCES, AND PEER OF THE REALM.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Loris" target="Four Kingdoms" id="0">
      <data key="d2">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.8</data>
      <data key="d4">Loris is close to the Foundation?” “Huh? Oh, you wouldn’t know. It’s one of the original Four Kingdoms.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FOUNDATION trilogy" target="Second Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d2">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">the FOUNDATION trilogy. This magnificently conceived series, winner of a special Hugo Award as Best All Time Series in the realm of science- and fantasy-fiction, is the finest imaginative creation in this field.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="First Foundation" target="outer periphery of the Galaxy" id="0">
      <data key="d2">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">It began as a small community of Encyclopedists lost in the emptiness of the outer periphery of the Galaxy.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="First Foundation" target="Hari Seldon" id="0">
      <data key="d2">PLANNED_BY</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">All had been planned by Hari Seldon, long dead now.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="First Foundation" target="barbarized planets" id="0">
      <data key="d2">TOOK_OVER</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">The First Foundation, with its superior science, took over the barbarized planets that surrounded it.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="First Foundation" target="Warlords" id="0">
      <data key="d2">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">It faced the anarchic Warlords that broke away from the dying Empire and beat them.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="First Foundation" target="Galactic Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d2">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">It faced the remnant of the Empire itself under its last strong Emperor and its last strong General and beat it.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="First Foundation" target="Search for the Second Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d2">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">The faithful of what was left of the First Foundation must find it for quite another reason.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Captain Pritcher" target="Mule" id="0">
      <data key="d2">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">the most useful was Han Pritcher, now lieutenant general.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Captain Pritcher" target="Democratic Opposition" id="0">
      <data key="d2">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">Han Pritcher had been a captain and a member of the underground Democratic Opposition.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Captain Pritcher" target="Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d2">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">In the days of the Foundation, Han Pritcher had been a captain</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Captain Pritcher" target="Foundation" id="1">
      <data key="d2">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">Captain Pritcher of the one-time Foundation.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Captain Pritcher" target="Conversion" id="0">
      <data key="d2">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">Until, that is, he was Converted.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Captain Pritcher" target="PERSON" id="0">
      <data key="d2">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">Captain Pritcher of the one-time Foundation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pritcher" target="Mule" id="0">
      <data key="d2">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">The huge, smooth door swung massively open at the general’s approach, and he entered.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pritcher" target="Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d2">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">Captain Pritcher of the one-time Foundation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bail Channis" target="Mule" id="0">
      <data key="d2">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">He was intelligent and self-possessed--therefore successful with the Mule.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bail Channis" target="Mule" id="1">
      <data key="d2">FRIENDS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d3">0.7</data>
      <data key="d4">He did not fear the mysterious Second Foundation. For that matter, he did not fear the Mule, and boasted of it.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bail Channis" target="Mule" id="2">
      <data key="d2">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">Bail Channis was one of these.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bail Channis" target="audience" id="0">
      <data key="d2">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">And now, for the first time, the Mule had summoned him to personal audience.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Palace" target="city" id="0">
      <data key="d2">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.8</data>
      <data key="d4">It brooded strongly over the empty grounds, over the crowded city on the horizon.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Kalgan" target="Union" id="0">
      <data key="d2">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.8</data>
      <data key="d4">the residence of the First Citizen of the Union, who ruled over an empire of his own.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Kalgan" target="Galaxy" id="0">
      <data key="d2">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d3">0.9</data>
      <data key="d4">Kalgan, more centrally located, with a long tradition as aristocracy’s playground</data>
    </edge>
